ept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-residue-odd"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-residue-odd"],"id":"long.thm-residue-odd","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.22 (Residue-class and odd-support irrationality)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.22, p. 50, label thm:residue-odd","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For integers $b\\ge2$, $m\\ge1$ and a residue $c$, $\\sum_{\\substack{n\\ge1\\\\n\\equiv c\\pmod m}}(b^n-1)^{-1}$ is irrational. Specializing $m=2,c=1$: $\\sum_{n\\text{ odd}} 1/(b^n-1)$ is irrational for every $b\\ge 2$, the case treated explicitly in \\[lucatachiya2017, Example 2, p. 140\\].*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.thm-residue-odd","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.thm-residue-odd","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.thm-residue-odd%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.irrational_erdosSupportSeries_odd%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.thm-residue-odd%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.irrational_erdosSupportSeries_odd%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.irrational_erdosSupportSeries_odd"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.thm-residue-odd","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.thm-residue-odd%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.irrational_erdosSupportSeries_residueClass%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f1904862